2026-10-28T17:48:59.1299419Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHy7M3UbKCM9boYpeP4kmC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 37,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/37\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"Inconsistent State on aws_lambda_function\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nterraform --version\\nTerraform v1.14.5\\non darwin_arm64\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/archive v2.8.1\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws v6.66.0\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/azuread v3.10.0\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/random v3.9.1\\n+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/time v0.14.2\\n\\nYour version of Terraform is out of date! The latest version\\nis 1.16.4. You can update by downloading from https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/install\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n* `aws_lambda_function`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nI expected a successful apply. It was only changing the timeout\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nIt didnt apply successfully, but reported a provider bug.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```console\\n\\u2502 Error: Provider produced inconsistent final plan\\n\\u2502 \\n\\u2502 When expanding the plan for module.agentcore.aws_lambda_function.tools_gateway_response_interceptor to include new values learned so far during apply, provider\\n\\u2502 \\\"registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws\\\" produced an invalid new value for .environment: block count changed from 0 to 1.\\n\\u2502 \\n\\u2502 This is a bug in the provider, which should be reported in the provider's own issue tracker.\\n```\\n\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\nConfiguration:\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_lambda_function\\\" \\\"tools_gateway_response_interceptor\\\" {\\n  function_name = \\\"${var.name}-tools-gateway-response-interceptor\\\"\\n  role          = time_sleep.tools_gateway_interceptor_role_propagation.triggers[\\\"role_arn\\\"]\\n  package_type  = \\\"Image\\\"\\n  image_uri     = local.base_container_image_uri\\n  architectures = [\\\"arm64\\\"]\\n  timeout       = 30\\n\\n  environment {\\n    variables = {\\n      GUARDRAIL_ID      = aws_bedrock_guardrail.tool_output.guardrail_id\\n      GUARDRAIL_VERSION = aws_bedrock_guardrail_version.tool_output.version\\n      # What the UI asks the user to authorize when a token exchange fails for\\n      # lack of consent: the app the gateway exchanges tokens with\\n      CONSENT_SCOPE = format(\\\"api://%s/.default\\\", azuread_application.agentcore.client_id)\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tags = merge(var.tags, {\\n    Name = \\\"${var.name}-tools-gateway-response-interceptor\\\"\\n  })\\n\\n  lifecycle {\\n    ignore_changes = [image_uri]\\n  }\\n\\n  depends_on = [\\n    aws_ecr_repository_policy.base_container_lambda_pull,\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis was the plan:\\n\\n```\\n# module.agentcore.aws_lambda_function.tools_gateway_response_interceptor will be updated in-place\\n  ~ resource \\\"aws_lambda_function\\\" \\\"tools_gateway_response_interceptor\\\" {\\n        id                             = \\\"agentcore-tools-gateway-response-interceptor\\\"\\n        tags                           = {\\n            \\\"Name\\\"    = \\\"agentcore-tools-gateway-response-interceptor\\\"\\n            \\\"Project\\\" = \\\"agentcore\\\"\\n        }\\n      ~ timeout                        = 3 -> 30\\n        # (30 unchanged attributes hidden)\\n\\n        # (3 unchanged blocks hidden)\\n    }\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\nOn next apply it applied successfully, so I cant say I could reproduce it\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand log output</summary>\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM 